-- title:
--   Tensor characters detect integers below exact-rank growth
-- statement:
--   For a field $F$, let $R_F(n)$ be the exact rank of the square matrix multiplication coefficient tensor of size $n$, and let $\nu_F=\inf_{n\ge2}\log R_F(n)/\log n$. Let $d,k\in\mathbb N$ with $d\ge2$ and $k<d^{\nu_F}$. Then there exists a tensor character $\chi$ such that
--   \[
--   k\le\chi(T_d).
--   \]
--   Here $T_d$ is the square matrix multiplication tensor, and a character is a nonnegative real-valued tensor invariant normalized at the scalar unit, additive under finite direct sums, multiplicative under tensor products, and monotone under restriction. This connects the actual rank exponent to bounds proved for all tensor characters.
-- source:
--   https://prove2.me/submissions/facf5b05-d302-42c1-a107-8ff40a0c2134; OAI.MatrixMultiplication.AuxiliarySeparation.exists_detecting_character, lines 8374-8394

